    "biography": {
      "concept": "Sergeant commanding the Eleven, the soldiers who came out of the Gift (Act 3)",
      "notes": "Sergeant Absalom Reyes commands the Eleven: eleven soldiers in immaculate parade uniform who rode inside the Gift and knocked before they came out, because their instructions said to, in writing. He has parade-ground courtesy and a card player's patience, answers exactly the question asked and no other, and salutes when unsure, which is often. He shuffles a deck of cards when he's thinking, and counts his men, eleven, every time a door opens."
    }
